<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>BDSP Data Publisher Guide</title>
    <script src="https://cdn.tailwindcss.com"></script>
    <style>
        @import url('https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Inter:wght@400;600;700&display=swap');
        body {
            font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif;
        }
        .flow-step {
            position: relative;
            padding: 1.5rem;
            background-color: white;
            border-radius: 0.5rem;
            box-shadow: 0 4px 6px -1px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1), 0 2px 4px -1px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.06);
            border: 2px solid #0047AB;
            width: 100%;
            max-width: 350px;
            text-align: center;
        }
        .flow-arrow {
            font-size: 3rem;
            line-height: 1;
            color: #0047AB;
            transform: rotate(90deg);
        }
        @media (min-width: 768px) {
            .flow-arrow {
                transform: rotate(0deg);
                margin: 0 1rem;
            }
        }
    </style>
    
</head>
<body class="bg-gray-100 font-sans leading-relaxed text-gray-900">

    <header class="bg-[#0047AB] text-white py-12 px-6 text-center shadow-lg">
        <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold mb-2">BDSP User Training</h1>
        <p class="text-xl md:text-2xl font-light">Guide for Data Publishers</p>
        <p class="text-lg font-light mt-2">data.gov.bt | 29th October 2025</p>
    </header>

    <main class="max-w-7xl mx-auto p-4 md:p-8">

        <section id="roles" class="mb-12">
            <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-center text-[#0047AB] mb-4">Who's Who: Platform User Roles</h2>
            <p class="text-lg text-center text-gray-700 max-w-3xl mx-auto mb-8">
                The BDSP platform defines three distinct roles, each with specific permissions. As a Data Publisher, you will primarily act as the "Data Focal."
            </p>
            <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
                
                <div class="bg-white rounded-lg shadow-md p-6 border-l-4 border-[#0047AB]">
                    <span class="text-4xl">👤</span>
                    <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mt-2 mb-2">Data Focal</h3>
                    <p class="text-gray-700">This is the primary data publisher. Your main responsibility is to create, manage, and publish datasets and their corresponding resources.</p>
                </div>
                
                <div class="bg-white rounded-lg shadow-md p-6 border-l-4 border-[#FFC300]">
                    <span class="text-4xl">🛠️</span>
                    <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mt-2 mb-2">Agency Admin</h3>
                    <p class="text-gray-700">The administrator for your specific agency. This user manages all member accounts and has the authority to add, edit, and delete entire datasets.</p>
                </div>
                
                <div class="bg-white rounded-lg shadow-md p-6 border-l-4 border-[#FF5733]">
                    <span class="text-4xl">👀</span>
                    <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mt-2 mb-2">Member</h3>
                    <p class="text-gray-700">A general user within your organization. Members have view-only access to the common and private datasets shared within your organization.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <hr class="border-t-2 border-gray-300 my-12">

        <section id="workflow" class="mb-12">
            <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-center text-[#0047AB] mb-4">The 2-Step Publishing Workflow</h2>
            <p class="text-lg text-center text-gray-700 max-w-3xl mx-auto mb-8">
                Publishing data is a two-part process. First, you create the "Dataset," which acts as a container. Then, you add "Resources," which are the actual data files.
            </p>
            
            <div class="flex flex-col md:flex-row items-center justify-center gap-4 md:gap-0 my-8">
                <div class="flow-step">
                    <span class="text-sm font-semibold text-gray-500">STEP 1</span>
                    <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold my-2">Create Dataset</h3>
                    <p class="text-gray-600">(The "Collection" or "Package")</p>
                </div>
                
                <div class="flow-arrow">➔</div>
                
                <div class="flow-step">
                    <span class="text-sm font-semibold text-gray-500">STEP 2</span>
                    <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold my-2">Add Resources</h3>
                    <p class="text-gray-600">(The "Actual Data" Files)</p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6 mt-10">
                <div class="bg-white rounded-lg shadow-md p-6">
                    <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4 text-[#0047AB]">Dataset Metadata Fields</h3>
                    <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">The Dataset holds the "who, what, and why" of your data.</p>
                    <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-2 text-gray-700">
                        <li><strong>Title:</strong> A clear, descriptive title.</li>
                        <li><strong>URL:</strong> A unique, auto-generated URL.</li>
                        <li><strong>Description:</strong> Provide detailed information about the content and purpose of the dataset. Markdown formatting is supported.</li>
                        <li><strong>Keywords:</strong> Add relevant keywords or tags separated by commas (e.g., health, economy).</li>
                        <li><strong>Data Focal (Organization):</strong> Select the organization responsible for managing this dataset.</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>

                <div class="bg-white rounded-lg shadow-md p-6">
                    <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4 text-[#0047AB]">Resource Metadata Fields</h3>
                    <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">Each Resource describes a specific data file.</p>
                    <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-2 text-gray-700">
                        <li><strong>Name:</strong> Descriptive name (e.g., "Jan 2021 Report").</li>
                        <li><strong>Description:</strong> Additional details (Markdown supported).</li>
                        <li><strong>Format:</strong> The file type (e.g., CSV, JSON, XLSX).</li>
                        <li class="font-bold mt-2">Two Ways to Add Data:</li>
                        <ul class="list-decimal list-inside ml-4">
                            <li><strong>Upload:</strong> From your computer.</li>
                            <li><strong>Link:</strong> From an external URL.</li>
                        </ul>
                    </ul>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-white rounded-lg shadow-md p-6 mt-8">
                <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-center mb-4">Resource Input Methods</h3>
                <p class="text-lg text-center text-gray-700 max-w-2xl mx-auto mb-6">
                    You have two options for adding your data resource: uploading a static file or linking to an external, live file.
                </p>
                <div class="flex flex-col md:flex-row justify-center gap-6 mt-6">
                    
                    <div class="p-6 bg-[#FFC300]/10 border-b-4 border-[#FFC300] rounded-lg w-full md:w-1/2 text-center shadow-lg">
                        <span class="text-6xl mb-3 block">⬆️</span>
                        <h4 class="text-xl font-bold text-[#0047AB]">Upload File</h4>
                        <p class="text-gray-600">From your computer.</p>
                    </div>
                    
                    <div class="p-6 bg-[#FF5733]/10 border-b-4 border-[#FF5733] rounded-lg w-full md:w-1/2 text-center shadow-lg">
                        <span class="text-6xl mb-3 block">🔗</span>
                        <h4 class="text-xl font-bold text-[#0047AB]">Link to URL</h4>
                        <p class="text-gray-600">From an external URL.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <hr class="border-t-2 border-gray-300 my-12">

        <section id="quality" class="mb-12">
            <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-center text-[#0047AB] mb-4">Ensuring Data Quality & Security</h2>
            <p class="text-lg text-center text-gray-700 max-w-3xl mx-auto mb-8">
                High-quality data is trustworthy data. Use schema constraints to enforce rules and masking to protect sensitive information.
            </p>
            <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-8 items-center">
                <div class="bg-white rounded-lg shadow-md p-6">
                    <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-center mb-4">Data Validation Constraints</h3>
                    <p class="text-gray-700 text-center mb-6">
                        Constraints are validation rules applied to data columns to ensure quality and consistency. The chart below shows the main types available.
                    </p>
                    
                    <div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-4 mt-6">
                        <div class="p-3 bg-gray-50 rounded-lg border-l-4 border-[#0047AB]">
                            <h4 class="font-bold text-[#0047AB]">Required</h4>
                            <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">Field must contain a value.</p>
                        </div>
                        <div class="p-3 bg-gray-50 rounded-lg border-l-4 border-[#FFC300]">
                            <h4 class="font-bold text-[#0047AB]">Unique</h4>
                            <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">All values must be distinct.</p>
                        </div>
                        <div class="p-3 bg-gray-50 rounded-lg border-l-4 border-[#FF5733]">
                            <h4 class="font-bold text-[#0047AB]">Minimum / Maximum</h4>
                            <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">Numeric range limits.</p>
                        </div>
                        <div class="p-3 bg-gray-50 rounded-lg border-l-4 border-[#C70039]">
                            <h4 class="font-bold text-[#0047AB]">minLength / maxLength</h4>
                            <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">String length limits.</p>
                        </div>
                        <div class="p-3 bg-gray-50 rounded-lg border-l-4 border-[#0047AB]">
                            <h4 class="font-bold text-[#0047AB]">Enum (Predefined List)</h4>
                            <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">Restrict values to a predefined list.</p>
                        </div>
                        <div class="p-3 bg-gray-50 rounded-lg border-l-4 border-[#FFC300]">
                            <h4 class="font-bold text-[#0047AB]">Pattern (Regex)</h4>
                            <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">Values must match a regex pattern.</p>
                        </div>
                        <div class="p-3 bg-gray-50 rounded-lg border-l-4 border-[#FF5733] col-span-2">
                            <h4 class="font-bold text-[#0047AB]">Mask (Sensitive Fields)</h4>
                            <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">Checkbox used to hide masked values.</p>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                
                <div class="bg-white rounded-lg shadow-md p-6 border-l-4 border-[#C70039]">
                    <span class="text-4xl">🔒</span>
                    <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mt-2 mb-3">What is Data Masking?</h3>
                    <p class="text-gray-700 text-lg mb-4">
                        Masking is a critical security feature.
                    </p>
                    <p class="text-gray-700">
                        When you check the "Mask" box for a specific data column (a schema field), its values will be hidden from view in the platform.
                    </p>
                    <p class="text-gray-700 mt-2">
                        This is essential for protecting sensitive or personally identifiable information (PII) while still acknowledging that the data field exists.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <hr class="border-t-2 border-gray-300 my-12">

        <section id="management" class="mb-12">
            <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-center text-[#0047AB] mb-4">Managing Your Published Dataset</h2>
            <p class="text-lg text-center text-gray-700 max-w-3xl mx-auto mb-8">
                Once your dataset is live, you can manage conversations with users via Discussions and follow best practices to keep your data relevant and clean.
            </p>

            <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-center mb-6">Managing Discussions</h3>
            <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6 mb-10">
                <div class="bg-white rounded-lg shadow-md p-6">
                    <h4 class="text-xl font-bold mb-3">Access Rules</h4>
                    <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-2 text-gray-700">
                        <li>Only <strong>logged-in users</strong> can view, create, or comment on discussions.</li>
                        <li><strong>Anonymous users</strong> will not see the Discussions tab or its contents.</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
                <div class="bg-white rounded-lg shadow-md p-6">
                    <h4 class="text-xl font-bold mb-3">Data Focal Privileges</h4>
                    <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-2 text-gray-700">
                        <li><strong>Delete Discussion:</strong> You can remove any discussion thread entirely.</li>
                        <li><strong>Close Discussion:</strong> You can close any open discussion, even if you did not create it.</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="pb-8">
                <a href="https://staging-admin.data.gov.bt" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
                    <button class="mx-auto block bg-blue-500 text-white px-8 py-3 rounded-lg text-lg font-semibold hover:bg-blue-600 transition-colors">
                        Walkthrough
                    </button>
                </a>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-white rounded-lg shadow-md p-6 md:p-8">
                <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-center mb-6">Data Focal Best Practices Checklist</h3>
                <ul class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-x-8 gap-y-4 max-w-4xl mx-auto text-lg">
                    <li class="flex items-start">
                        <span class="text-green-500 mr-3 text-2xl">✅</span>
                        <span>Use <strong>clear, descriptive titles</strong> for datasets.</span>
                    </li>
                    <li class="flex items-start">
                        <span class="text-green-500 mr-3 text-2xl">✅</span>
                        <span>Provide <strong>detailed descriptions</strong> using Markdown.</span>
                    </li>
                    <li class="flex items-start">
                        <span class="text-green-500 mr-3 text-2xl">✅</span>
                        <span>Include <strong>relevant keywords</strong> and tags.</span>
                    </li>
                    <li class="flex items-start">
                        <span class="text-green-500 mr-3 text-2xl">✅</span>
                        <span>Select appropriate <strong>categories and licenses</strong>.</span>
                    </li>
                    <li class="flex items-start">
                        <span class="text-green-500 mr-3 text-2xl">✅</span>
                        <span>Use <strong>consistent file formats</strong> (e.g., CSV for tabular data).</span>
                    </li>
                    <li class="flex items-start">
                        <span class="text-green-500 mr-3 text-2xl">✅</span>
                        <span>Define schema fields with clear <strong>titles and types</strong>.</span>
                    </li>
                    <li class="flex items-start">
                        <span class="text-green-500 mr-3 text-2xl">✅</span>
                        <span>Apply <strong>constraints</strong> (required, unique, etc.).</span>
                    </li>
                    <li class="flex items-start">
                        <span class="text-green-500 mr-3 text-2xl">✅</span>
                        <span>Use <strong>masking</strong> for sensitive fields.</span>
                    </li>
                    <li class="flex items-start">
                        <span class="text-green-500 mr-3 text-2xl">✅</span>
                        <span>Use clear <strong>version identifiers</strong> (e.g., v1.0, v2.0).</span>
                    </li>
                    <li class="flex items-start">
                        <span class="text-green-500 mr-3 text-2xl">✅</span>
                        <span>Update version notes with <strong>meaningful change logs</strong>.</span>
                    </li>
                    <li class="flex items-start">
                        <span class="text-green-500 mr-3 text-2xl">✅</span>
                        <span>Use <strong>discussions</strong> to clarify dataset issues.</span>
                    </li>
                    <li class="flex items-start">
                        <span class="text-green-500 mr-3 text-2xl">✅</span>
                        <span><strong>Close resolved discussions</strong> to maintain clarity.</span>
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </section>

    </main>

    <footer class="bg-gray-900 text-white text-center py-8 mt-12">
        <p class="text-lg">Thank You</p>
        <p class="text-lg font-bold">༄ འབྲུག་གཞུང་འཕྲུལ་རིག་ལས་སྡེ། | GovTech Bhutan</p>
    </footer>

    <script>
        window.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {
        });
    </script>
</body>
</html>
